<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch diagnose second case of &quot;mad cow&quot; disease.</title>
<headline>Dutch diagnose second case of &quot;mad cow&quot; disease.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands on Monday reported its second case of bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE) or mad cow disease.</p>
<p>The Agriculture Ministry said the disease had been diagnosed in a six-year old cow in the northern province of Friesland which was slaughtered in late March. The ministry said both the farm and the slaughterhouse had been sealed off.</p>
<p>BSE is a brain-wasting disease which has been linked to a new strain of the fatal Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease in humans. The Netherlands' first case was reported in March.</p>
</text>
